<p>SYNAPTICA is a neuroscience website in Spanish and English that updates itself every day: science news with verified summaries and sections to learn how the brain works. It is meant both for curious people without training and for students.</p>
<h2>Who we are</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Sofía</strong>, PhD student in neuroscience: reviews the scientific content.</li>
  <li><strong>Aday</strong>, data engineer: builds the site.</li>
</ul>
<h2>How it is made</h2>
<p>It reuses the «engine» of <a href="https://adaycuestacorrea.github.io/paleo-atlas/en/index.html" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Paleo Atlas</a>. It costs nothing: it runs on free services and on language models whose texts are checked before they are published. The code is free software (AGPL-3.0) and our texts are CC BY-SA 4.0.</p>
